1 HINTS

   The topics, by subject.  Type HELP and a topic's name for more.

2 Files_and_volumes

     BACKUP          List, restore, compare, or save BACKUP save sets
     CONVERT         Copy a file's records into another organization
     COPY            Copy files between the host and mounted volumes
     CREATE          Make a file, a directory, or a logical name table
     DELETE          Delete files on a mounted volume
     DIRECTORY       List files on a mounted volume
     DISMOUNT        Detach a volume from its device
     DUMP            Show a file's blocks or records
     EDIT            Edit a file with an editor on the host
     INITIALIZE      Make a container volume, or the machine's memory
     MOUNT           Attach a container to a device
     PURGE           Delete all but the newest versions of files
     RENAME          Rename or move files on a mounted volume
     SPECIFY         How a file is named: a volume's or the host's
     TYPE            Show a file at the terminal

2 Command_procedures

     @               Run a command procedure
     CALL            Run a subroutine of a procedure
     DECK            Make data lines that start with "$"
     EXIT            End a procedure, or govax at the terminal
     GOSUB           Run the commands at a label, then come back
     GOTO            Go on at a label
     IF              Run commands when an expression is true
     INQUIRE         Ask the terminal for a symbol's value
     Lexicals        F$ functions: the process, files, strings, time
     ON              Choose what a failing command does
     Symbol_Assign   Symbols, expressions, and $STATUS
     WAIT            Wait for a time

2 Files_in_procedures

     CLOSE           Close a file OPEN opened
     OPEN            Open a file for READ and WRITE
     READ            Read a record into a symbol
     WRITE           Write a record

2 Logical_names

     ASSIGN          Make a logical name, equivalence first
     DEASSIGN        Delete logical names
     DEFINE          Make a logical name, or a device
     SHOW            SHOW LOGICAL and SHOW TRANSLATION

2 Programs

     ANALYZE         Describe an object file, an image, or an RMS file
     FORTRAN         Compile FORTRAN into MACRO-32
     LIBRARY         Make and change libraries
     LINK            Link objects into an image
     MACRO           Assemble MACRO-32 into an object
     MCR             Run an image with a command line
     FOREIGN         Run an image as a command
     RUN             Run an image

2 Processes

     ATTACH          Give the terminal to another process
     LOGOUT          End a subprocess
     SPAWN           Make a subprocess
     STOP            End procedures, or delete a process
     SHOW            SHOW SYSTEM, SHOW PROCESS, SHOW WORKING_SET

2 The_machine

     ASM             Assemble into memory, before the microkernel
     CLEAR           Clear memory or the string pool
     DEBUG           Start the debugger
     LOAD            Load a ROM or NVRAM image
     PRINT           Show expressions in the console's radix
     PSL             The processor status longword
     SAVE            Save a ROM or NVRAM image
     SET             The console's settings
     SHOW            The machine's and the console's state
     TIME            Time a command
     VMINIT          Lay out virtual memory
     XFC             govax's extended function codes
     ZERO            Clear memory

2 govax

     ABOUT           Who made govax
     CONFIGURATION   govax's settings, and how to set them
     KEYS            Ctrl/C, Ctrl/Y, and Ctrl/Z
     QUIT            Leave govax
     STARTUP         What govax does as it starts
     SYSTEM_VOLUME   The volume of govax's own files
